  "body": "Owed from #110 (branch issue/110-pause-home, stacked on PR #147).\n\n#110 shipped the per-operation \"After this operation\" action (Continue / Optional stop / Program stop / Go home), a per-op Suppress toggle, and a post option \"Skip pauses and homes\". The issue also asked for Pause and Home as **standalone entries** in the operation list, placed between operations.\n\nWhy it was left out: every program walk assumes an operation has a tool and a toolpath - `posting::program_ops` (tool gate, freshness), `rest::ahead_of`, the program sim, the setup sheet and the tool list. An entry with no toolpath needs either its own entity kind threaded through those walks, or a carve-out in each of them. That was more than the #110 timebox could take. The per-op action already produces the same NC.\n\nDone means: a Pause and a Home entry can be added from the operation list's context menu, reordered like an op, and undone. They post the same words as the per-op action (`PARAM AfterOperation` or an equivalent record), honour Suppress and \"Skip pauses and homes\", round-trip through the project file, and never hold the post as \"not generated\".\n",
